# Spaghetti Checker — One Context Per File

Keep each file focused on a single responsibility. Too much in one file (TMI) hurts
readability, reviewability, and testability.

**Enforcement:** `pnpm run check:spaghetti` (also in Husky pre-commit and Cursor
`afterFileEdit` / `stop` hooks). Fix all violations before declaring work done.

---

## Canonical module layouts

### Backend — `apps/api/src/modules/<name>/`

```
<name>/
  handlers/              # one handler per route action
    list-*.handler.ts
    create-*.handler.ts
    index.ts
  schemas/               # one schema per file
    *.schema.ts
    index.ts
  __tests__/             # all tests here — never beside source
    *.service.test.ts
    *.handlers.test.ts
  <name>.routes.ts       # thin wiring only
  <name>.service.ts
  <name>.repository.ts
```

| File | Allowed contents |
|------|------------------|
| `*.routes.ts` | Router + middleware + `asyncHandler(namedHandler)` |
| `handlers/*.handler.ts` | Single exported handler function |
| `schemas/*.schema.ts` | Single Zod schema; import `z` from `core/openapi/zod` |
| `*.service.ts` | Business logic; no HTTP types |
| `__tests__/` | Vitest tests only |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — inline handler
commentsRoutes.get('/projects/:id/comments', asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  res.json(await commentsService.listByProject(req.params.id))
}))

// ✅ GOOD
commentsRoutes.get('/projects/:id/comments', validate({ params }), asyncHandler(listProjectCommentsHandler))
```

Shared handler helpers (e.g. session cookies) → `handlers/_shared/` or dedicated file.

### Frontend — `apps/web/src/modules/<name>/`

```
<name>/
  components/            # one React component per .tsx
  hooks/                 # one hook per file
  pages/                 # route-level page components
  api/                   # typed API client for this feature
  lib/                   # module-specific utils
  store.ts               # Zustand slice (optional)
  routes.tsx             # re-exports pages only — no component bodies
  __tests__/             # Vitest tests only
```

| File | Allowed contents |
|------|------------------|
| `routes.tsx` | `export { XPage } from './pages/x-page'` only |
| `pages/*.tsx` | Single page component |
| `components/*.tsx` | Single component (or single hook if in `hooks/`) |
| `hooks/*.ts` | Single custom hook |
| `__tests__/` | Vitest + Testing Library tests |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — page defined in routes.tsx
export function ProjectsPage() { return <div>...</div> }

// ✅ GOOD — routes.tsx
export { ProjectsPage } from './pages/projects-page'
```

Cross-feature imports go through `lib/`, `components/ui/`, or public module surfaces —
never another module's internals.

---

## When to split

Split when a file has **more than one** of: handler, schema, service concern, React
component, page, or hook.

---

## Tests

All tests live in `__tests__/` — never co-located beside source.

```
modules/comments/
  __tests__/
    comments.service.test.ts
    comments.handlers.test.ts
```

API target: ≥ 80% statement coverage (`apps/api/vitest.config.ts`).
Web target: ≥ 80% on tested UI components (`apps/web/vite.config.ts`); tests are
Testing Library only in `__tests__/*.test.tsx`.

---

## Agent checklist (run on every module create/modify)

When creating or editing anything under `apps/api/src/modules/` or
`apps/web/src/modules/`:

1. **Match layout** — use the canonical folder tree above.
2. **Split before merge** — new route → new handler file; new schema → new schema file; new page → `pages/`.
3. **Run checker** — `pnpm run check:spaghetti` must pass.
4. **Run gates** — `pnpm run typecheck` and `pnpm run test` for touched apps.
5. **Update docs** — `docs/BACKEND.mdc` or `docs/FRONTEND.mdc` if module structure changed.

If the checker fails, fix structure — do not disable or bypass the rule.
